---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import BabyNamePopularity from '@/components/tools/reference/BabyNamePopularity.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="baby-name-popularity">
  <BabyNamePopularity client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to use the baby name popularity tool</h2>
    <p>
      Type up to three names, separated by commas, and choose girls or boys. The chart shows the rank of
      each name in each year since 1880; switch to babies to see how many children got the name. The
      table gives the latest rank, the best rank and the year it happened, and the number of babies
      since 1880.
    </p>
    <h2>Where the data comes from</h2>
    <p>
      The US Social Security Administration counts the first names on applications for Social Security
      cards. It publishes every name given to at least five babies of one sex in a year, and adds the
      past year each May. Rank 1 is the most common name of that year; equal counts are ranked by the
      order SSA lists them in.
    </p>
    <h2>Reading the trend</h2>
    <p>
      Rank shows popularity against other names; the number of babies also follows the number of births,
      which changed a lot over the century. Spellings count as separate names, so a name that is spread
      over several spellings looks less popular than it sounds. The tool includes every name that was in
      the top 1,000 of its sex in at least one year.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
